{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And Terah died in Haran.</b> He did not exert himself to attain what they had intended to attain in setting out from Ur of the Chaldeans, nor did he come at all to Abraham while he was in the land of Canaan and called there on the name of HaShem, despite the greatness of his name at that time. The opposite of this Lot did for a time, and therefore he and his seed merited a certain portion of Abraham's gifts — whereas the rest of Terah's descendants, as closely related to Abraham as he or more, did not merit this."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:50.047818145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}